0M11936 2066h0M12411 1613h0M12168 1689h0M12806 1120h0M12703 1200h0M12682 1268h0M12852 1984h0M13280 5526h0M12670 4873h0M12761 4972h0M12636 5052h0M12574 5201h0M12582 5313h0M12949 1347h0M12971 1242h0M13015 1059h0M12954 1083h0M12577 1419h0M12654 1408h0M12874 1192h0M11924 1823h0M18464 4874h0M19119 4624h0M18649 5527h0M6264 3376h0M6965 3761h0M7073 3840h0M7239 3762h0M7387 3898h0M7808 4236h0M8148 3441h0M7430 3075h0M7246 1660h0M7178 1510h0M6064 1862h0M1034 6767h0M1535 8233h0M19378 7831h0M13634 1222h0M14132 950h0M14132 950h0M13210 953h0M13406 760h0M13574 785h0M13831 749h0M13790 781h0M13650 893h0M13565 976h0M16906 2722h0M17212 2740h0M16310 2653h0M15970 2281h0M18391 3242h0M18602 4082h0M18481 4017h0M17783 3344h0M10973 4526h0M10701 3759h0M10678 4461h0"/></svg><figcaption><span class="map-key"><i class="k-p"></i>Profile</span><span class="map-key"><i class="k-s"></i>State</span><span>342 states with a known seat in 1956</span><a href="/atlas?year=1956">Open the atlas at 1956 &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/british-empire"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/British%20Empire.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>British Empire</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Suez Crisis exposes Britain's inability to act against US wishes</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/united-kingdom"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/United%20Kingdom.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>United Kingdom</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Suez Crisis exposes the limits of British power</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/hyderabad-state"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Hyderabad%20State.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Hyderabad State</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Hyderabad State is divided on linguistic lines</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/united-state-of-rajasthan"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/United%20State%20of%20Rajasthan.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>United State of Rajasthan</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Ajmer and Mount Abu are added and the office of Rajpramukh abolished</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/french-west-africa"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/French%20West%20Africa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>French West Africa</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The loi-cadre Defferre gives power to elected territorial assemblies</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/buddhism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Buddhism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Buddhism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">B. R. Ambedkar and hundreds of thousands of his followers become Buddhists at Nagpur</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-egypt"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Egypt.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Egypt</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Nasser becomes president in June, the last British troops leave the Canal Zone on 13 June, and on 26 July he nationalises the Suez Canal, provoking the Suez Crisis.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/islamic-republic-of-pakistan"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Islamic%20Republic%20of%20Pakistan.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Islamic Republic of Pakistan</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Pakistan adopts a republican constitution and becomes an Islamic republic with two geographically separate provinces, East Pakistan and West Pakistan.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/environmental-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Environmental%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Environmental movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Britain passes the Clean Air Act after the Great Smog of 1952 in London</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/non-aligned-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Non-Aligned%20Movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Non-Aligned Movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Tito, Nehru and Nasser sign the Declaration of Brijuni in Yugoslavia</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/social-democracy"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Social%20democracy.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Social democracy</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Anthony Crosland’s The Future of Socialism argues that traditional capitalism has been reformed almost out of existence</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/dead-sea-scrolls"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Dead%20Sea%20Scrolls.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Dead Sea Scrolls</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Cave 11 yielded the last fragments found near Qumran, among them the Temple Scroll</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/democratic-republic-of-vietnam"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Democratic%20Republic%20of%20Vietnam.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Democratic Republic of Vietnam</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Hồ Chí Minh apologises on 18 August for the errors of the land reform, and rioting against its excesses breaks out in a largely Catholic district in November</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/khartoum"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Khartoum.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Khartoum</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Khartoum becomes the capital of independent Sudan</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/mona-lisa"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mona%20Lisa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mona Lisa</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A rock thrown by Ugo Ungaza Villegas shattered the glass case and dislodged a speck of pigment near the left elbow</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/b-r-ambedkar"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/B.%20R.%20Ambedkar.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>B. R. Ambedkar</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Converts to Buddhism at Nagpur and then converts some 500,000 of his supporters</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/b-r-ambedkar"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/B.%20R.%20Ambedkar.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>B. R. Ambedkar</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Dies in his sleep at his home in Delhi on 6 December</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/mau-mau-rebellion"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mau%20Mau%20rebellion.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mau Mau rebellion</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Field Marshal Dedan Kimathi is captured on 21 October, ending the British military campaign</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/marxism-leninism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Marxism%E2%80%93Leninism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Marxism–Leninism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Khrushchev denounces Stalin's cult of personality at the 20th Congress of the Soviet party</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/stalinism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Stalinism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Stalinism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Khrushchev’s Secret Speech condemns Stalin’s cult of personality at the Twentieth Party Congress</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/african-socialism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/African%20socialism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>African socialism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Abdoulaye Ly publishes Les masses africaines et l'actuelle condition humaine, the first influential socialist text tailored for Africa</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/juche"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Juche.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Juche</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A failed challenge to Kim Il Sung's leadership leads to a purge of pro-Soviet and pro-Chinese elements from the Workers' Party of Korea</span></li></ul></section>
